 # Framework API drift: methods LG's 2016 Ims4 calls that were renamed on A17. old|new (same signature).
 Landroid/telephony/SubscriptionManager;->getSlotId(I)I|Landroid/telephony/SubscriptionManager;->getSlotIndex(I)I
+# A17 removed PhoneStateListener(int subId); drop to no-arg super (subId now lives on the TelephonyManager)
+invoke-direct {p0, p2}, Landroid/telephony/PhoneStateListener;-><init>(I)V|invoke-direct {p0}, Landroid/telephony/PhoneStateListener;-><init>()V
+# --- Stale com.android.internal.R.bool resource IDs ---
+# LG's 2016 ImsManager/ImsCall/ImsGlobal baked compile-time com.android.internal.R.bool IDs; resource
+# IDs shift every Android release, so these throw Resources$NotFoundException on A17. Remap each stale
+# 2016 id -> the current A17 id for the same-named config bool (looked up in framework-res.apk).
+# 0x112008e (config_carrier_volte_provisioning_required) has no A17 bool; point it at a valid bool
+# (config_carrier_volte_available) so it never throws -- provisioning is not gated for this bringup.
+0x112008a|0x01110311
+0x112008b|0x01110307
+0x112008c|0x01110143
